Way back in the mists of time, on Nethack 3.0j, I had not ascended.  My best
game...

Hakichi-San the Samurai was doing well on his quest to recover the Amulet.
Wandering about, he sought the stairwell which would take him to the
Medusa level, when beneath him, the floor opened.

You fall into a pit!  --More--           [I shrug.  Big deal]
You fall onto several spikes!  --More--  [Who cares?  Plenty of hit points.]
The spikes were poisoned!  --More--      [Well, there goes the strength, I guess.]
The poison was deadly!  --More--         [Oh no...]
You die.

After several futile hours of screaming and beating my head against a wall,
I started again.

Months passed.

Then, another good game:

Hagumba was doing well.  He stomped about the level, easily dispatching monsters
which stepped in his way.  He was seeking the stairs to the Medusa level when
a ghost popped up.  Undaunted, Hagumba engaged it in combat; within several
minutes, the former adventurer's spirit was put to rest.  And there, clearly
visible, the former adventurer's possessions lay in a forlorn heap.  Hagumba
thinks, This good; other adventurer must be tough, like me, to get this far!
He must have lot good stuff; me get spoils of war!  He steps onto the pile, and...

You fall into a pit!  --More--          [Deja vu!]
You fall onto several spikes!  --More-- [OH NOO!!!!!! Not again!!!]
The spikes were poisoned!  --More--     [Ah shit...]
The poison doesn't seem to affect you.

I tell you, I've never been so grateful for Barbarian's intrinsic poison
resistance...

